  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What changed",
      "items": [
        "A new command starts Leglas on a practice app, opens it in a hidden browser and counts what it does",
        "Each count has one saved limit; going over fails, and raising a limit takes a written reason"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What stayed the same",
      "items": [
        "Leglas itself: no product code changed",
        "The everyday tests and checks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "ELI5",
      "items": [
        "Before this change, nothing counted the work Leglas does when it starts or while it sits open, so a heavier version could ship without anyone noticing.",
        "Now every proposed change starts Leglas on a practice app, counts the programs it starts and the requests it makes, and fails if any count goes over its saved limit.",
        "Each improvement becomes a floor that later changes cannot quietly undo."
      ]
    }
  ]
